  "level": "2",
  "url": "nagata-interpolation.html#nagata-plane-fields",
  "type": "Corollary",
  "number": "6.4",
  "title": "",
  "body": " Let be an uncountable algebraically closed field of characteristic zero. For every , the strict inequality of holds outside a countable union of proper closed subsets of , with nonempty complement.  The incidence loci in are defined over by minors of the matrices of Taylor coefficients. Whenever , the corresponding locus is proper over by . A nonzero rational defining minor remains nonzero under field extension, so the locus is proper over . Exclude these loci for the countably many violating pairs . Because is uncountable, it contains elements algebraically independent over : at each successive choice the algebraic closure of the field generated by the preceding elements is countable. Using them as affine coordinates gives a tuple avoiding every excluded locus and every diagonal. This proves .  "
